---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="The same small turn sweeps a greater distance on a distant wall">
  <SvgFigure
    name="lighthouse-beam"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg"
    viewBox="0 0 470 250"
    title="Light rays from a turning lighthouse hit two possible walls"
    desc="Two rays leave a lighthouse at slightly different angles. Their points of contact are close together on a nearby wall and much farther apart on a distant wall. Each ray travels outward from the lighthouse."
  >
    <g fill="none" stroke={series.gold} stroke-width="3">
      <path d="M45 120 L445 24" />
      <path d="M45 120 L445 216" />
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke={stroke} stroke-width="3">
      <path d="M205 60 V180" />
      <path d="M445 15 V225" />
    </g>
    <g fill={series.red} stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1.5">
      <circle cx="205" cy="81.6" r="6" />
      <circle cx="205" cy="158.4" r="6" />
      <circle cx="445" cy="24" r="6" />
      <circle cx="445" cy="216" r="6" />
    </g>
    <g fill="none" stroke={series.blue} stroke-width="2.5">
      <path d="M224 81.6 H238 M231 81.6 V158.4 M224 158.4 H238" />
      <path d="M406 24 H420 M413 24 V216 M406 216 H420" />
    </g>
    <g fill={series.blue} font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="231" y="202">
        Small sweep
      </text>
      <text x="356" y="243">
        Much larger sweep
      </text>
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="205" y="18">
        Near wall
      </text>
      <text x="405" y="18">
        Far wall
      </text>
      <text x="45" y="165">
        Light
      </text>
      <text x="45" y="183">
        source
      </text>
    </g>
    <path d="M33 116 L45 91 L57 116 Z" fill={series.gold} stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1.5" />
    <circle cx="45" cy="120" r="6" fill={series.gold} stroke={stroke} stroke-width="1.5" />
  </SvgFigure>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    If the wall is sufficiently distant, the bright spot can sweep across it faster than light.
    <strong> No object or signal travels sideways between spots:</strong> different photons
    travel outward to each part of the wall. The rays show two positions of the beam, not a
    single photon changing course.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
